  prose(<<~'CANONICAL_CHRONICLE', origin: :published)
    # THE ACCORD OF BEACON LIGHT AND DEEP FIRE
    ### Between the Faction Holdborn (ice-thresh) Aurora-Chartered, and the Guild Weal' Clique~ of Nightfall Shelf, Concerning Joint Stewardship of The Beacon Stack
    
    ---
    
    ## PREAMBLE
    
    WHEREAS the collapse of the Tertiary Spire at The Dawn Terrace claimed the lives of Qingyaieifu (void-banisher), Shanfongqongja Teir'Gleam, and Ouchangzhaijun (thaw-survivor, Echo: Xe), and WHEREAS the succession crisis thereafter designated Frost-heir (line-severed) demonstrated that contested territorial claims, left unresolved, produce not governance but graves;
    
    WHEREAS the predations of the orca war-pods have rendered independent defense of outlying resource nodes insufficient to sustain either signatory through the coming Long Dark;
    
    WHEREAS the Stillness-Bound charter, as amended under the seventeenth and twenty-third addenda ~~and the thirty-first~~ [*clause struck; ink discolored; original terms illegible beneath commemorative witness-marks for the Thaw-Paths dead*], provides the legal framework under which resource obligations between Aurora-descended and Nightshelf-descended factions may be adjudicated;
    
    WHEREAS both parties acknowledge the fire-core supply crisis renders separation untenable, and WHEREAS neither party names the cause;
    
    The signatories hereby bind themselves before witnesses present and *witnesses beyond the signatories*, under observation of those who attend but do not sign.
    
    ---
    
    ## ARTICLES OF ACCORD
    
    **Article I — Joint Stewardship of The Beacon Stack.** Holdborn (ice-thresh) citing claim through seizure during the Great Thaw and authenticated by Sholong's Codex, shall maintain surface governance of The Beacon Stack's harvester platforms and Slide Prism refineries. Weal' Clique~ shall maintain subsurface operations including corruption-monitoring of degraded crystal spires and deep-ice stabilization, pursuant to stewardship expertise as recognized under the Accord of Still Pools and Frost Zenith.
    
    **Article II — Aurora-Crystal Harvest Quotas.** The seasonal crystal harvest shall be divided: three-fifths to Holdborn (ice-thresh) for surface-trade and Long Dark stockpiling; two-fifths to Weal' Clique~ for Glow-Fissure containment operations and Nightshelf infrastructure. ~~One-tenth reserved for the Frost-heir's household~~ [*provision retained as memorial; no household survives to claim it*]. The clause that remembers the dead shall not be amended.
    
    **Article III — Corruption Containment.** Weal' Clique~ shall provide quarterly corruption-assessment of The Beacon Stack's compromised crystal facets, including those spires where the ice-rot has dulled aurora-resonance and spread through support beams in patterns no practitioner will classify aloud. Holdborn (ice-thresh) shall supply fire-cores sufficient to power containment wards, at a rate of no fewer than four cores per assessment cycle. [*Provision restored from lapse under Stillness-Bound, Article 9, fire-core warranty terms requiring three-day replacement of defective cores.*] What neither signatory will name presses against the crystal from within. Containment is acknowledged as delay, not cure.
    
    **Article IV — Garrison and Mutual Defense.** Each signatory shall maintain a garrison of no fewer than twelve armed penguins at The Beacon Stack during the Long Dark. Garrisons shall occupy separate platform sectors. Neither garrison shall approach the other's sector without courier-delivered written authorization, sealed under Stillness-Bound precedent.
    
    **Article V — Courier Inviolability.** All accord-runners carrying sealed confirmations between signatories shall be inviolable under terms established by the Flipper Accord. Interference with accord-runners shall be punished by exposure, as precedented by the seventeen skeletons at Midway Shelf—cited not as warning but as standing sentence.
    
    ---
    
    ## ENFORCEMENT & DURATION
    
    This accord shall endure for a period of four Long Dark cycles, renewable by mutual consent. Violations shall be adjudicated by the Courier Corps under Stillness-Bound precedent. Should either signatory breach Articles I through IV, the aggrieved party may petition the Courier Corps for binding arbitration. Should arbitration fail, the accord dissolves, and all provisions revert to the terms of Stillness-Bound as they existed before this layer was added—if such terms can still be read.
    
    ---
    
    ## SIGNATURES
    
    Signed under observation at The Beacon Stack, in the fourth week of the Long Dark, by the light of aurora-crystals placed as bond-lights at the signing table—which dimmed, though neither delegation acknowledged this.
    
    **Gilt-Hand Yeaiu qi'Gleam**, Codex-Bearer of Holdborn (ice-thresh) who drew blood from her left flipper upon the ☽'micseleia' Dagger and pressed it to the page. The seal split where the blade's fracture ran. Both parties note the imperfection.
    
    **Crypt-Chancellor Silvcaeclerae-fawn~**, of Weal' Clique~, who drew blood upon the same blade and pressed it beside the first. The ancestor-bone hilt was warm. She did not hold it long.
    
    The ☽'micseleia' Dagger was returned to silk. Its fracture is wider now.
  CANONICAL_CHRONICLE
  annotation "note_1771585223427_0", anchor: "under observation of those who attend but do not sign", text: "Signed in the fourth week of the Long Dark, when the boundary between the living world and ice-memory is thinnest. At a site dense with aurora-crystal — which concentrates residual light, and concentrates what gathers near residual light. Weal' Clique~ knew what attends at crystal concentrations when the veil thins. The Nightshelf always know. That the bond-lights dimmed and neither delegation acknowledged it tells me the watchers were expected, or at least unsurprising. This is not diplomatic metaphor. This is a treaty co-signed by presences neither faction will name in writing.", type: :commentary, display: :full
  annotation "note_1771585223427_1", anchor: "One-tenth reserved for the Frost-heir's household", text: "Three-fifths plus two-fifths plus one-tenth equals eleven-tenths of the harvest. The Frost-heir's share was drawn from somewhere — the text never specifies whose portion it diminished. Now that the provision survives only as memorial, the question is moot. But someone drafted an accord promising more crystal than existed, and both signatories signed it. I have learned not to be surprised by this.", type: :pedantic, display: :popout
  annotation "note_1771585223427_2", anchor: "WHEREAS neither party names the cause", text: "They both know. The geological collapses are not secret — they are simply inconvenient to state in a document that asks both parties to trust each other's supply commitments. Holdborn cannot admit their fire-core access is failing. Weal' Clique~ cannot admit how much they know about why.", type: :skepticism, display: :popout
